spec ww13-void-property-delete-lpg: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW13, property arm, through the lpg API: DelNodeProperty is a void primitive: a conflict it hits cannot be returned by the
# statement, so it is RECORDED on the transaction and must surface at COMMIT as a
# serialization conflict, applying nothing (F3, rmp #2354). A COMMIT that succeeds
# after a recorded conflict is a silently dropped write.

starting permutation: s1x s1c s2x s2c
step s1x: lpg: DelNodeProperty(n, p)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2x: lpg: DelNodeProperty(n, p)
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
ERROR: serialization conflict
final final: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) RETURN n.p AS p
p   
----
null
(1 row)

